+
+	A presenter thread waits for the GPU and reads the frame back, while the
+	GL thread goes on with the next frame, into the other buffer: the GL
+	thread waits only until the presenter is done with the frame before. A
+	GL thread holding the view's window (one that draws in Draw(), say)
+	reads the frame back itself: the presenter couldn't show it before the
+	window is free again.
 */
